nodecode-calling-mom is a rewrite of SlyBase's SlyBase/calling-mom:

  https://github.com/SlyBase/calling-mom
  commit e0daf7f1b293cdf41b685f856b02120f82c144d9
  MIT, Copyright (c) 2026 SlyBase (LICENSE)

Rewritten: the two tiers and their instruction texts (__init__.py's
_PROMPTS and the ESCALATE gate), the risk lists and their two levels
(rules.py, reordered and trimmed to the patterns that survive a reading),
the stuck signals and the result fingerprint that makes them measurable
(signals.py), the egress redaction including the password-in-a-URL case
(_core.redact_for_egress plus the plugin's own _URL_CREDS), the NO_ACTION
silence, and the second_opinion tool (handle_second_opinion and
_SECOND_OPINION). All of it now speaks through one model seam,
NLE:COMPLETE, so the cell carries no HTTP client, no credentials and no key
of its own.

Left out, and why: the Kanban board itself. The original's budgets live in
task comments, its advice is a comment on a card, and its strongest
behaviours - pinning a [crit] card to a model, handing a [review] card to a
reviewer, gating kanban_complete on a verify: line, sweeping parked cards
from cron, the completion check against a card's summary, the Pushgateway
metrics - all read or write that board. A Nodecode session has no card, so
a budget is counted in calls, advice is a line appended to the tool result
that provoked it, and the sweep, the completion check, the [crit] and
[review] markers and the metrics have no counterpart. The signals the
original derived from a worker run became two the one :TOOL point can
measure: the identical call three times within ten (loop), and the
identical result three times in a row (same_result, the original's
same_error), whose fingerprint normalizes paths, hex and numbers away.
The setup, status and doctor subcommands became one /calling-mom command, and
Advanced Delegation's model routes are not read: mom and olymp are named as
provider/model in the section.
